WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.360
"Kodomo no Omocha"

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.890
and your bitter face and bitter
feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.350
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.860
I may be a little jumbled,
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.950
Take-chan...

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.530
Take-chan...

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.800
He seems to have settled down.
He's okay now.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.920
Really?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.470
Although, he will need
to rest in bed for a while.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:07.100
Hey, they said you're all right.
You surprised me.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.820
From now on, I'm going to oversee
your nutrition, okay? Get well soon, now.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.030
"What did the doctor
and Mama talk about?"

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.030
Hmm... it couldn't be...

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:24.160
Yes, he does appear to require some rest,
but for now, he seems to be all right.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.500
He's still asleep right now.
Um... what will you do about the taping?

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.210
Oh, it's all right, it's all right.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.090
We were thinking of having Take-san
die off in that scene.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.420
We're re-writing the script now.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.390
Well, you know, the name
of the show is "Chaos Theater,"

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.100
so it will probably
be lost in the confusion.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.100
Well, take care.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.900
You don't have to... kill him off...

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.610
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.110
Huh? I can't stay here?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.450
Let's let the doctors take care
of him tonight, and go home.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.780
I wonder if it would be okay if I stayed
until Take-chan opens his eyes.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.700
Take-chan doesn't have any family,

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.450
and he'll probably feel lonely
if no one is here when he wakes up.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.460
You are the one and only family he has!
Ah, what am I thinking!?

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.790
What's the matter, Mama?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.000
I'm okay, just let me be.
Anyhow, let's go home.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.800
Tomorrow is another day.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.800
"Tomorrow" is written as "brighter day."
Isn't that nice, isn't that nice?

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.810
Take-chan, I'm going home now.
I'll see you again tomorrow, okay?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.100
Take-chan...

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:38.110
You'll be okay, Take-chan.
You've still got your life ahead of you.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.450
The happy times have finally come,
after all.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.780
See, it's just like I told you, right?
You just have to keep working at it now.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.080
Take-chan, you just have to see
"Chaos Theater" through to the end.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.460
Okay, Take-chan?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:57.090
"This Is Our Last Scene Together"

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.470
He doesn't have any! That man
does not have any tomorrows!

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.810
If I don't get him to announce
that he is her father now,

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.810
then it's going to end for them like this,
without them knowing anything!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.440
T- that's okay! That would be okay!
It's better like this, without them knowing!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.150
What would they do if they did know!?

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.610
I heard that guy fell ill.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.830
Nicely evaded!

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.290
What is this, Hong Kong cinema?

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.080
Word sure does travel fast, huh?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.080
So? How is his condition?

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.080
Nothing much. Just a prolapsed stomach.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:37.750
Prolapsed stomach?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.760
He ate too much watermelon,
and his stomach prolapsed.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.760
Not a very witty joke, was it?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.760
A prolapsed stomach from
eating watermelon isn't too swift.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.430
Boo on you too, Pops!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.100
Maybe you're right.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.770
You're going to look
into it anyway, right? Here.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.770
This is your consideration for earlier,
and some hush money.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.110
Is it that bad?

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.650
Do not go near those two for a while.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.780
Rei-kun, what's going on with the drama?

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.790
Oh, they said not to worry. It sounds like
they're re-writing the script for Gojo-san.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.120
Really? That's terrific.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.130
I can't wait to see the script
for the last episode.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.130
I- I can't tell her...

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.630
I can't tell her...

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:40.520
"An anguished Mama and Rei-kun"

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
Wow, everyone is troubled, huh?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.130
Yo!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.130
We're friends, right?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:27.800
I guess.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.470
Since when?

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.470
I need a favor.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.810
W- what is it?

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.720
Go swipe Gojo-san's chart for me.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.730
That wouldn't be right!

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.730
Maybe I should hiss at you.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.520
A- all right. We are friends, right?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.740
Ordinarily, Babbit isn't supposed to
get involved in the story, you know...

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.070
Let's see... Gojo... Gojo...

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.490
Oh, I get it. Anything is okay,
as long as Babbit does it.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.790
That handwriting looks like a snake
slithered through there, huh Snake?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.330
"Thinking up something else nasty?"

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.370
You're thinking up
something nasty to do, huh?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.090
This was lying over there.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.090
T- this is Gojo-san's chart!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.090
That shouldn't happen.
That's something important, right?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.090
How?

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.760
Say, is he going to die?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.430
Well, it's written right there.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.430
T- there's no way something like that
would be written on his chart!

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.100
Then I'm right?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.230
Thank you.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.020
"That was a bad thing to do!!"

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.020
Listen up, that was a bad thing to do!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.110
Sana-chan, what is that!?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.120
A thousand paper crane's
worth of paper in one crane!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.080
I can't fold up that many of them,
so I combined them all into one!

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.750
Is that even what a crane looks like?

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.750
Boom!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.750
S- Sensei, are you doing
a thousand paper cranes, too?

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.630
Mm-mm, I just wanted to run into you.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.430
Take-chan!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.770
You're awake!

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.430
Take-chan?

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.100
Are you alive?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.810
Wouldn't this usually be bad?

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.400
"Let's just say we're glad
he came around..."

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.400
We'll cut that out later.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.780
Take-chan, how are you feeling?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.450
I'm a little bit groggy,
but I seem to be okay.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:15.120
Ah, that really is great.
You startled me last night.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.450
Surprised you?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.790
I can't take that, okay?
I absolutely cannot take it.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.120
I can't take it, either.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.040
Hurry and get better, okay?

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.800
You're finally starting to get
good roles coming your way now.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:31.130
Oh, right, what happened to
"Chaos Theater" on location last night?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.050
They suspended everything
where it was yesterday,

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:38.060
but now, I heard they were
re-writing the script for you, Take-chan.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.730
Really? I'm glad to hear that.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.400
Everyone is counting on you, Take-chan.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.730
I mean, you've got the co-starring role
in that Golden Drama next, right?

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:51.400
You got yourself a big role!
After that, things will pick up in a hurry!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.410
Boom, boom, boom, like that! And your
popularity is going to skyrocket, too!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.740
You'll be working like crazy
as a movie star.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.080
From serious roles...

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.830
...to variety.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.080
Movies, huh?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.420
That would be a dream.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.420
It's no dream.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.420
This is no dream.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:15.220
It's going to come true. Really.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:24.100
Whoa, but before that happens, you can't
Ignore your work on "Chaos Theater," sir.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.110
You've got to keep working at everything.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.440
Right.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.440
Hang in there until the end, My Darling.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.740
Yes, my daughter.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.530
Now then, now that I've seen
my daddy's happy face, I can relax.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.410
Your daughter should go to school!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:41.750
Come see me again, my daughter.
Don't desert your dad.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.040
As soon as I can.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.420
Ka-ching!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.710
As if I'd desert you! We'll be together
the rest of our lives, Take-chan!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:56.470
We'll be together the rest
of our lives, so brace yourself!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:01.890
"Flesruoy ecarb!" What was that?

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.850
It was "brace yourself!"

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:08.940
Wha-!?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.490
"My dad died"!?

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:14.650
"Sana-chan now exploding with anger"

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.280
Mister Tsu!!

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.620
You know, for some reason, as I
wear these costumes day after day,

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.910
I think I might keep puhforming
like this forevuh.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.580
These othuh charactuhs are
bettuh at portraying humans.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.960
Ah, Sana-chan!

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.630
Yet it always seems to come down
to this punchline, huh?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.920
Squished flat, huh?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.880
Ah! The snake is stomping in
with his shoes still on!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.880
I want to be treated like a human being!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.220
Why!? Why!? Why does Take-chan die!?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.220
No! There's no way you can do that!

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.890
You were all saying such good things
about Take-chan before, weren't you!?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.560
You were praising him for getting
so much better, weren't you!?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.230
That is true, but with
Gojo-san in the hospital...

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.570
No!!

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.570
Re-write it! Re-write the script
so that Take-chan comes through!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.900
S- Sana-chan!

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.240
What are you doing!? Calm down!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.910
No! Tsu is an idiot! He's a lowlife!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.330
You've gone too far!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.910
Apologize to him, Sana-chan.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.580
Apologize.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.250
But...

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.250
Sana-chan,

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.590
Tsu-san was thinking of Gojo-san when
he dropped him from "Chaos Theater."

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.510
If he pushes himself too hard now,

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:20.590
Gojo-san will be burned out
for his upcoming Golden Drama, right?

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:25.600
Right now, it's more important
for Gojo-san to rest easy and recover.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.270
Gojo-san should place his stake
in his upcoming, bigger job, right?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.610
Isn't that better for him, Sana-chan?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.610
But...

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.280
I can well appreciate how you feel,
Sana-chan,

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.150
but what would be best for Gojo-san?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.370
What would be best for Gojo-san?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.870
I'm sorry, Tsu-san.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:52.210
No... I don't mind... just move the desk...

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.880
Move the desk, please...
Sana-chan... Sana-chan?

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.800
"The Dream Goes On Forever"

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.880
Sana-chan, here.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.550
I went and got the scripts
for Gojo-san's new drama.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.890
How about you go give them to Gojo-san?
He'll be thrilled, won't he?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.560
Take-chan's Golden Drama scripts?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.900
Rei-kun!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.570
Thank you, Rei-kun! I love you!
I'm going to go show these to Take-chan!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.570
Yahoo!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.570
That was a sweet thing to do,
wasn't it, former boyfriend?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:24.240
She kissed me! It's been so long
since she kissed me on the cheek!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.700
Keep playing the handsome lover through
to the end once in a while, why don't you?

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.580
Hayama!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.250
Yo!

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.590
Don't you "yo" me.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.920
Hey, Hayama, what kind
of face am I making?

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.590
The same moronic
happy-go-lucky face as always.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:46.260
You don't say. Same as always, huh?
You don't say, you don't say.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.020
Thank you, Hayama!

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.560
"Resolve"

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.610
Oh, there's a firm subtitle.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.940
Doing better?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.280
Still sick.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.950
What's this here?

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.280
The Golden Drama script.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.620
Rei-kun went and got them for me.
Take-chan, this is a really good part!

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.290
You get to steal the main character's
girlfriend away from him.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.960
You get a lot of... how shall I say...
presence with it.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.960
And the role of the girlfriend is
being played by Kobayashi Noripi!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.590
That's so great! This is definitely
going to build your reputation!

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.960
Right? Right, Take-chan?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.970
Right? So, you know, Take-chan...

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.970
So, you know... so...

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:31.480
...maybe you shouldn't work so hard
on "Chaos Theater," you know?

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.770
You should put your stake
in the Golden Drama.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.270
"Chaos Theater" is just a two-bit program,

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.280
and it's not the sort of drama
you should be ruining your health over.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.950
Did they drop me?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.360
It's not like that.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.950
Tsu-san also said you should rest up
and get behind the Golden Drama,

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:52.290
that it would be the best thing
for you to do, Take-chan.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.620
I think that's definitely
the best thing to do, too.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.670
After all... after all, Take-chan,
you've got a dream.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.960
You've got a dream coming your way.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.220
Right now, just think
about this Golden Drama,

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:07.090
and forget about "Chaos Theater."
Okay, Take-chan?

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.810
Mm-hmm, all right.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:20.650
I can't believe it. This kind of job
really did come my way, huh?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.900
It really did. It really, really did.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.990
I think I'm really starting
to feel like working!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.990
It took you long enough, Take-chan!
Of course you do!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.660
Oh, sorry.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.910
Take-chan!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.910
There is one thing I have to tell you.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.920
Yes?

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.040
Stay with me forever.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.590
I will stay with you forever.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.590
Really?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.260
Really.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.890
I need you.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.260
I got that!

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:54.270
"I need you. I need you. I need you."

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.270
"Uoy deen I. Uoy deen I"

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.270
Huh? That's not very funny.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.400
It's not something that should
be funny when reversed.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:05.400
"Sana-chan sings"

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.610
We've been using this sign
since the first episode, huh?

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:05.610
♪ Tomorrow is the day after today! ♪

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.610
♪ The day that is today
is all for tomorrow, ♪

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.620
♪ the day after, the next day,
and the day after that! ♪

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.620
♪ However far you go, it never ends. ♪

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.950
♪ There is no end to the days
we call tomorrow. ♪

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:14.950
--♪ We're together today, ♪
--♪ We're together today, ♪

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:15.950
--♪ and we'll be together tomorrow, ♪
--♪ and we'll be together tomorrow, ♪

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:16.960
--♪ so we'll be together ♪
--♪ so we'll be together ♪

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:17.960
--♪ for the rest of our lives! ♪
--♪ for the rest of our lives! ♪

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.960
--♪ So we'll be together ♪
--♪ So we'll be together ♪

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.960
--♪ for the rest of our lives! ♪
--♪ for the rest of our lives! ♪

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.960
Keep it down, you bastards!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.420
What kind of idiot makes
a huge commotion in a hospital,

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.300
you nitwits!?

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.300
Seems like I've seen that guy before...

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.970
That's right.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.930
Today, tomorrow, the next day...
our time together will go on forever.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.600
I'm a real "poemer."

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.980
Today, tomorrow, the next day,
our time together will go on forever!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.610
"A 'poemer' is someone
who writes poems... I think"

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.650
A "poemer" is someone who writes poems.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.280
Hi there.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:46.900
Don't "Hi there" me!

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.700
My name is Kurosaki,
and I'm a free entertainment reporter.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.240
Pleased to meet you.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.620
An entertainment reporter?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.910
Among entertainment reporters,

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.620
there are good reporters
and bad reporters.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.960
Of the two, I am a good reporter.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.290
Ah, you're a fine one to talk!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.540
You're not a fine one,
you're not a fine one...

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.670
"What happens when a snake reporter
visits you in the hospital?"

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.710
You sure are quick to put the hiss on!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.300
Having an unknown actor of the same age
as myself suddenly become popular...

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.300
...would be quite a delightful topic for me.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.640
I would love to gather
some more information.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:15.640
You mean about the Golden Drama?
Word gets around fast.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.640
That's my job.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.930
I see.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:21.650
Now, would you tell me
what you are thinking right now?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.270
Are you planning to make this
into an article for after Gojo-san dies?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:25.320
Is that so wrong?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.440
Of course it's wrong!

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.820
"I've shown you another bad thing to do"

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.440
Maybe I should just give up

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.820
trying to keep this anime
geared toward good boys and girls.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:33.240
I'm thinking that
this sort of thing does happen.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.580
When one door closes,
another one is opened.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:41.580
I'm going to stake
my whole life on this drama.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.250
My whole life, in which everything
I've done has been left unfinished.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:50.590
What about "Chaos Theater"? That is
your breakout show, right, Gojo-san?

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.590
Yes. This drama has given me
much to think about.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:57.260
Particularly meeting Kurata Sana-chan.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:01.270
People have said all sorts of things
about our relationship,

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.600
but she is quite an extraordinary girl.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.610
She's beyond extraordinary.
I can't even put it into words.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:08.940
What about "Chaos"?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.950
I've been taken out of it. Or, to be
more precise, I've been dropped from it.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.950
But it might work out
to be a positive thing for me.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.620
I'll be able to take my time working out
my next role in the meantime.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.620
What have you told Kurata Sana?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:27.630
She's the one who suggested
that I should get plenty of rest now,

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:28.960
and think about the future.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.550
Kurata... Kurata said that?

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:37.930
I think she's right. A role
this big is a first for me-

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.890
Kurosaki-san?

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:48.230
You are such a damned fool...

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:53.240
You're... going to end up
leaving things unfinished...

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:58.240
I happen, Gojo-san, to know
Kurata Sana quite well.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.910
She's an incredible girl.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.920
She's incredible... You don't
even hold a candle to her...

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.250
And you're her father!

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.590
No, I'm not-

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:14.930
Sakai Keiko, the woman you abandoned...

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:17.260
...is also...

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:20.930
...Kurata Sana's real mother.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.610
Kurata loves you. She wants
to be with you, forever!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.230
Can't you do anything for her?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:36.910
For the daughter who loves you,
now, at the end?

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.240
You're on your way to dying!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:42.620
You're going to die,
and leave things unfinished!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.260
What are you doing, Snake!?

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:58.260
My age has caught up to me.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:58.930
What?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.260
I'm giving this back.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.720
What!?

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:12.940
Kurosaki, just this once, I...

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.400
...thank you.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:18.950
Okay, Sana-chan, this is the last out.
Let's make it a good one, okay?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.620
R- right.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.620
Okay, once this is finished, we'll have a
wrap party at the conveyor-belt sushi bar!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.620
Ready...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.620
Ah, I seem to have gotten better.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.960
T- Take-chan?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.290
T- Take-san, what are you doing here?

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:34.550
Oh, they gave me a shot, and I got better.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.210
You're better?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:41.090
Director, would you let me play the part
of the father protecting his daughter,

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.220
as originally planned?

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.560
No, we can't do that.
We've already shot everything else.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.230
Well then,

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.890
please re-write the script
and shoot it again.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.900
We don't typically do that.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:55.150
This isn't typical.
I'm betting my life on it.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.860
Huh? What are you saying?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.580
Yeah, okay, I guess you're right.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.910
Writer!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.290
I never liked this last scene
to begin with!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.250
Re-write it the way
it was originally planned!

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.920
Y- you're kidding me!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:12.920
Take-chan...

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.550
Wow, how embarrassing.
They said I was just vitamin deficient.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.920
Sorry to worry you, Sana-chan.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.590
Huh? Really?

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.590
Yes. It seems so dumb.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.260
It seems ridiculously dumb.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:28.560
Yeah, it seems dumb. But look,
they gave me a vitamin shot this huge,

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.600
so I'm feeling great.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.900
Surprised you?

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:32.900
0 points.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.190
Ah, after all this, still 0 points?

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:39.740
"The script is re-written"

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.570
Okay, it's re-written.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.780
Something's wrong if you
can re-write it that easily.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.030
Take-san, this might be a bit hard on you,
with you on the mend. Are you okay?

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.530
I'm betting my life on it!

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.910
All right, ready...

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.870
Start!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.960
--Run, Yumi!
--Dad!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:52.250
Okay!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:54.920
--Are you okay?
--Mm-hmm.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.040
Start!

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.260
Okay!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.590
Start!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:03.970
Okay!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.220
Start!

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:09.890
Dad, I'm scared!
Stay by Yumi's side always!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:13.270
I will be!
I'll be by your side forever, Yumi!

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.610
Cut! Okay! Okay, Take-san!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:20.280
I'll be by your side forever, Yumi...
forever...

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.740
Take-chan?

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:26.240
--Take-san, that was amazing!
This drama is going to be amazing!
--Thanks.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.240
We're going to do the last scene now.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.620
Let's do it.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.290
The unseen enemy's searchlights
are closing in,

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.210
and the dad holds Yumi and jumps.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.540
The light hits the wall
of the warehouse,

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.550
and as the dad holds his daughter,
and the daughter holds her dad,

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.130
forever holding tightly to each other,
into the happy ending!

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.210
Ooh, I'm going to cry!

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.880
Ready, start!

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:43.550
Dad!

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.800
Yumi! Hold on tight!

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:51.100
Now jump!

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:04.360
I made it... the last scene...

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:11.240
For the first time in my life...
I saw something through to the end...

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.250
Take-chan...

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:19.420
I'm sorry, Sana-chan... Just once...

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:22.260
I wanted to see something
through to the end...

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.590
Even if it were fake...

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:29.260
even if it were fake, I wanted to see
what it was like to protect my daughter...

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.260
Take-

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:32.600
I made it...

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:36.940
At the end, I finally made it...
at the end...

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.770
Take-chan...

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.530
Sana...

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:47.950
D- Dad?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:54.750
I'm so glad... I met you...

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.760
Take-chan?

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:08.890
Take-chan?

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.930
No... not yet...

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:18.650
No... Take-chan...

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:23.980
No...

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:25.650
No!

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:27.990
Not yet!

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:30.660
You can't die yet!

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:35.750
No!

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:38.790
It's all DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:41.590
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:43.710
Bye Bye Bye

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.380
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:48.340
and your body will be healthy,

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.180
so resolve when to give up

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:52.140
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:53.470
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken)

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:55.180
(Tidak apa-apa,
Nday kambay kambay)

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:57.770
It's always the same old nonsense,

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:00.230
U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:02.810
(Mm? Could be you're fairly dumb...)

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:05.480
and then later comes the whimpering,

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.320
KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:10.780
(Ah... it's fine, it's fine, it's fine)

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:13.070
It's all crazy over there,

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:14.990
it's all "waah!" over here,

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.330
and the whole Earth
is spinning the wrong way.

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:22.170
So at this point now, yeah at this point now,

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:26.460
you can laugh it away, excuse me, I must be going.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.380
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.220
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.140
Bye Bye Bye

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:35.970
Cuz you tried your MECHA-KUCHA best,

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.890
to PECHA-KUCHA out a "Hi,"

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.850
so just keep going unlike this!

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:41.730
Wai Wai Wai Wai

00:23:41.850 --> 00:23:43.650
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:43.770 --> 00:23:48.530
Once your lips touch, you can't change your mind.

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:51.240
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.110
and your body will be healthy,

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:55.080
so resolve when to give up

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:58.660
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:00.870
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken,
Tidak apa-apa)

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:02.830
(Gwaenchansseumnida,
kwenchanayo)

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:04.250
(Mou man tail)

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:17.390
Take-chan, isn't this great?

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:22.850
I'm not the only one...
who remembers you, Take-chan.

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:31.320
...who knows that you
lived a full life, Take-chan...

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:37.450
"Spring Comes In an Avalanche of Tears"
